      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no distinct \"type\" of melanoma categorized by race; the biological mechanisms of the tumor are fundamentally the same regardless of the patient's ethnicity. The observed differences are primarily due to later stages of diagnosis driven by restricted in situ detection capabilities in darker skin types, combined with higher risks of developing acral lentiginous or mucosal melanomas which behave more aggressively. Therefore, the approach should focus on recognizing these less common, high-risk presentation sites rather than assuming a different molecular subtype. Structured surveillance and rigorous teaching in diverse patient populations remain the key strategies to mitigate these disparities.",
